Give terrestrial LocationReport a json factory and construct it through it

Dev accepted, in these words: "Build the LocationReport json factory with both terrestrial sites
re-authored" — the recommendation being to give LocationReport its drake surface with the `json`
factory, re-canonicalize its JSON, replace its hand-written Scala with the generated file,
re-author both terrestrial construction sites as `LocationReport(payload)` and regenerate them,
and add one LocationReportTest covering exact trio agreement, a lazily evaluated factory
argument, and a codec round-trip of the json; the three sibling reports to follow by the same
pattern as the next increment.

The point the Output repair left in view: five definition sites construct a report the same way,
as the host-opaque string `new X { override lazy val typeDefinition = X.typeDefinition; override
lazy val json = payload }` — terrestrial Output and the four OriginateReports — because the four
report types (terrestrial LocationReport, aerial PositionReport, marine FixReport, ethereal
EphemerisReport) were JSON-only definitions with no drake surface, no elements and no factory:
`type X from <Medium> draco format dracon Dracon` and nothing more. A Dracon carries `json`, and
Dracon's own factory is `par json Json`; a derived report with the same factory is the natural
constructor — in Haskell, `LocationReport :: Json -> LocationReport` over the parent's payload.

Probed with the compiled CLIs before recommending. The surface

    type LocationReport from Terrestrial draco format dracon Dracon
      factory
        parameters
          par json Json
    domain domains terrestrial Terrestrial

parses, emits back clean, and generates a companion with `apply(_json: => Json)` binding
`override lazy val json`, a Dracon-shaped encoder and decoder, and `Null = apply(Json.Null)`,
importing `io.circe.{Decoder, Encoder, Json}` exactly as Dracon's companion does. The BARE
spelling `Json` is the one HostBindings carries and Dracon.drake authors; the qualified
`io.circe.Json` spelling generates a Null of `null.asInstanceOf[io.circe.Json]` and a strict
decoder, and was not used. Re-authoring the two terrestrial sites as `fix report LocationReport
LocationReport(payload)` — a positional call the parser trees as `{"()": ["LocationReport",
"payload"]}` — regenerates OriginateReport.scala and Output.scala with exactly that one line
changed each: `lazy val report: LocationReport = LocationReport(payload)` in the rule action,
`val report: LocationReport = LocationReport(payload)` in the strict case branch. No engine
change. The hand constructions in tests (`new domains.aerial.PositionReport { … }`) stay valid
Scala; a factory invalidates none of them.

Built as probed: LocationReport.drake is new (the first drake surface in the corpus for a report
type), LocationReport.json is the compiled DrakeCLI's re-canonicalization (the factory record
added, nothing else moved), LocationReport.scala is the compiled GeneratorCLI's output replacing
the hand-written companion, which it extends rather than alters (the trait, the three kind-vals
and the loader line are unchanged). `DrakeCLI check` over terrestrial: surface drift 0, json
drift 0. LocationReportTest (3) pins the trio (emit, parse, generate, the factory's one
parameter named json typed Json, parents Terrestrial then Dracon), the by-name argument
(evaluated zero times until the first read of `json`, once after, never again; the instance is a
Terrestrial and a Dracon; Null's json is Json.Null) and the codec (`asJson` is `{"json": payload}`,
decoding reads the report back, an empty object decodes to Json.Null). The existing terrestrial
OriginateReportTest and OutputProjectionTest pin the two regenerated sites by exact agreement
with their files, so they gate this regeneration without change.

